It is Friday evening, and Nina knocks on my door.
She has her dog, Ludwig, with her.
He is going to stay with me for the weekend.
Nina smiles and gives me the leash.
"Thank you so much for the help, Maya," she says.
"It is absolutely fine," I answer happily.
She explains a few things to me about him.
"Give him food at seven in the morning and at six in the evening," Nina says.
"And remember, he must not have human food."
I laugh and look down at the little dog.
"No, Ludwig, my dinner is not for you," I say to him.
Nina laughs too and points at the door.
"Always keep him on the leash when you walk close to the big road," she says.
"In the park he is allowed to run freely."
I nod.
"Don't worry, I will take good care of him."
Nina hugs me and says goodbye to us.
She closes the door, and I stand alone with Ludwig.
He looks up at me and wags his tail.
I am already very fond of him.
